   "data": {
    "path": "product/pilot-shop.md",
    "title": "The Pilot Shop: the walkthrough's product",
    "body": "# The Pilot Shop: the walkthrough's product\n\n*An authored example, made up for this demo: the Pilot Shop is no one's shop, and its people are named by their seat. It\nshows what a team's project holds once its AI has filled the product side, and one request's whole loop.*\n\n## The product\n\n- **Three apps:** the Storefront (the website), the Shop app (mobile) and the Back office (the shop team's admin). Each\n  screen on Map · Screens carries its wireframe.\n- **One API:** eleven doors on Map · Doors, each with the screens that call it and the tables it reads and writes.\n- **One database:** six tables on Map · Data (customers, products, orders, order_items, invoices, payments) with their keys,\n  and the three things the product talks about (a customer, an order, an invoice).\n- **The connected apps:** the payments provider, the email service and the CRM, on Map · Arch with what reaches each.\n- **Two flows** on Map · Flows: a shopper pays by card; a business buyer pays by invoice.\n- **Two open decisions** on Map · Deps: the invoice's payment terms, and the first reminder's day, which waits on them.\n\n## The loop, one request end to end\n\n1. **Proposed.** A business seat files the request (lane BA, a proposal) on the goal *Pilot Shop: a business buyer pays by\n   invoice*: business buyers asked to pay on invoice with a PO number. A proposal waits for the owner.\n2. **Decided.** The owner approves it, with the reason.\n3. **Picked up.** A developer takes its next action: it is theirs until done.\n4. **Filed done.** The developer files the change (lane code) on the same goal, with its proof.\n5. **Graded.** A tester grades the checks it must pass, each with its proof; the screens and doors they name light up.\n6. **Announced.** Marketing files the launch (lane GTM) on the same goal, with the outcome it expects.\n\nThe goal's page shows each lane's cell move: the business ask, the build and the launch, beside the checks' grades.\n",
    "asOf": "2026-10-10",
    "confidence": "direction"
   }
  }
 ]
